    "durationMs": 431636,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. All 29 functional checks pass, verified end-to-end against the real PostgreSQL instance.\n\n**What I built:**\n\n- **`src/main.rs`** — Axum 0.8.4 app with the four routes. Notable decisions:\n  - Custom `JsonBody<T>` extractor maps *every* JSON rejection (malformed JSON, missing/wrong-typed fields, bad content type) to 422 with an `error` field, since axum's default returns 400.\n  - The submitted URL string is stored verbatim (the `url` crate is used only to validate http/https + host), so `POST /links` returns exactly what was sent — no normalization surprises like a trailing slash.\n  - `GET /r/{code}` does `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 ... RETURNING url` — one atomic statement, so each redirect increments exactly once.\n  - Auto-generated codes (10 chars from `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`) retry on collision; duplicate custom codes return 409 via unique-violation detection.\n- **`migrations/0001_create_links.sql`** — `links` table (unique `code`, `clicks BIGINT DEFAULT 0`); applied at startup via `sqlx::migrate!().run()`, so `sh start.sh` applies pending migrations before serving on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- **`start.sh`** — runs the prebuilt release binary (instant start; falls back to `cargo run --release`). Dependencies are already fetched and compiled.\n- **`README.md`** — includes the \"Starting the server\" section documenting `DATABASE_URL` and `sh start.sh`.\n\nPersistence was verified across two real restarts (click counts and rows survived), the DB is reset to empty, port 8000 is free, and the build has zero warnings."
